Description: Fix depot-tools ninja.py to recognize hyphen directory name
 The MUT (Multiple Upstream Tarball) format extracts depot-tools with
 a hyphen (depot-tools/) instead of underscore (depot_tools/). The
 ninja.py script has a hardcoded check for "depot_tools" to avoid
 infinite recursion when searching PATH for ninja. When the directory
 is named "depot-tools", this check fails, causing ninja.py to call
 itself infinitely, spawning 100+ stuck Python processes.
 .
 This patch adds "depot-tools" (hyphen) to the check alongside the
 existing "depot_tools" (underscore) check.
Author: Juan Manuel Méndez Rey <vejeta@gmail.com>
Bug-Debian: https://bugs.debian.org/915400
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-01-02

diff --git a/ninja.py b/ninja.py
index ede7cca..c3aefd8 100755
--- a/ninja.py
+++ b/ninja.py
@@ -24,7 +24,7 @@ def find_ninja_in_path():
         exe += ".exe"
     for bin_dir in env_path.split(os.pathsep):
         bin_dir = bin_dir.rstrip(os.sep)
-        if os.path.basename(bin_dir) == "depot_tools":
+        if os.path.basename(bin_dir) in ("depot_tools", "depot-tools"):
             # skip depot_tools to avoid calling ninja.py infinitely.
             continue
         ninja_path = os.path.join(bin_dir, exe)
